      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "HFrEF:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " reduces all-cause mortality and should be considered in all HFrEF patients; preferred over an ACE inhibitor or ARB if tolerated, with early switching supported even in hospital."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start 49/51 mg BID if previously on an ACE inhibitor or ARB; 24/26 mg BID if on a low dose, ACE-I/ARB-naive, or with low/borderline BP. Double after 2 to 4 weeks to the target 97/103 mg BID as tolerated. Patients on an ARB can switch with no washout."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "K-sparing diuretics, K supplements or K-containing salt substitutes may raise serum K; lithium toxicity has been reported with ARBs, so monitor lithium levels."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Overdose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hypotension is the most likely result; treat symptomatically."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
